  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Boil the kettle. Half-fill a medium saucepan with boiling water.<br>• Cook udon noodles over medium-high heat, gently stirring with a fork to separate, until tender, 1-2 minutes.<br>• Drain, rinse and set aside.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d82d0118d6e477003fc9e9/step-f3265100.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Meanwhile, roughly chop Asian greens. Slice lime into wedges. Cut plain firm tofu into 2cm chunks.<br>• In a large frying pan, heat a generous drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.<br>• When the oil is hot, cook tofu and trimmed green beans, turning occasionally, until browned, 5-6 minutes (cook in batches if your pan is getting crowded).</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d82d0118d6e477003fc9e9/step-26966310.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Add ginger lemongrass paste and satay seasoning and cook until fragrant, 1 minute.<br>• Stir in Asian greens, coconut milk, plant-based fish sauce, the soy sauce and a splash of water. Simmer until slightly reduced, 1-2 minutes.<br>• Gently stir in cooked udon noodles, baby spinach leaves and a good squeeze of lime juice, until combined, 1 minute. Season to taste.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d82d0118d6e477003fc9e9/step-3cd95b20.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Divide tofu and coconut curried noodles between bowls. <br>• Serve with any remaining lime wedges. Enjoy!</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d82d0118d6e477003fc9e9/step-f7a19b30.jpg"
    }
  ]
